---
// PRIVACY POLICY. Describes what the code actually does (keep it in sync when data handling changes). It's a plain-
// language draft written alongside the engineering: have it reviewed by a lawyer before launch, and set
// PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL so readers can reach you.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const contact = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL as string | undefined;
const updated = "27 October 2026";
---

<Layout title="Privacy — Clipbench" description="How Clipbench handles your files and data.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 text-body leading-relaxed sm:px-6 [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-h3 [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_li]:mt-1 [&_p]:mt-3 [&_ul]:mt-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6">
    <h1 class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-body-sm text-(--color-text-muted)">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Editing runs on your device.</b> The files you edit stay in your browser. They aren't uploaded when you trim, caption, export or use the on-device AI tools (transcription, background removal, Clean Audio, stem separation and the rest).</li>
      <li><b>Cloud AI features are optional.</b> Only when you run one does what that feature needs leave your device. You're told what first, and uploaded media is deleted within 24 hours.</li>
      <li>No ads, no trackers, no selling or sharing your data, and nothing you send is used to train AI models.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>On your device</h2>
    <p>Projects, autosaves, version history, your brand kit and your settings are stored in your browser (IndexedDB, Cache Storage and localStorage). They stay there until you clear them. AI models for the on-device tools are downloaded from Hugging Face and jsDelivr, which see your IP address like any website you visit.</p>

    <h2>Cloud AI features</h2>
    <p>Some features (for example dubbing, voice cloning, AI images and script writing) run on our servers. When you run one:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>What's sent:</b> exactly what that feature needs, such as the text you entered, or the voice sample or video you chose. The feature's notice tells you before the first use.</li>
      <li><b>Uploaded media</b> (audio, video, images) is stored privately and <b>deleted within 24 hours</b> after the job finishes.</li>
      <li><b>Job records:</b> the content of a job (what you sent and what came back) is <b>deleted after 30 days</b>. We keep a minimal record (which feature, when, credits used and its cost to us) to run the daily free credits and prevent abuse.</li>
      <li><b>Processors:</b> Supabase (database, sign-in and file storage, hosted in India) and the AI provider that runs the feature, such as Anthropic, fal.ai or Modal. They process data only to provide the feature, under their own terms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accounts and credits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An account is optional. If you sign in, we store your <b>email address</b> to send sign-in links and keep your daily credits. Your browser keeps the sign-in session.</li>
      <li>Without an account, your free daily credits are tied to a <b>one-way, salted hash of your IP address</b>. We never store the address itself.</li>
      <li>To stop automated abuse, cloud AI requests pass a <b>Cloudflare Turnstile</b> check, which Cloudflare runs under its own privacy policy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Stock library:</b> your search terms go to Pexels, Pixabay or Openverse through our server. Files you import come through our server and are processed on your device.</li>
      <li><b>Link transcription:</b> when you paste a link, our server downloads its audio once to transcribe it, then deletes it.</li>
      <li>Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs (IP address, time, page) for security for a short time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use everything without an account, and without cloud features, if you prefer.</li>
      <li>Delete local data by clearing this site's data in your browser.</li>
      <li>Ask us to delete your account and records{contact ? <>: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="underline">{contact}</a></> : " via the contact address shown on this site"}.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Clipbench isn't directed at children under 13, and cloud features require you to be old enough to agree to these terms where you live.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll update the date above and say so on the site.</p>
    <p class="mt-8 text-body-sm"><a href="/terms" class="underline">Terms of use</a> · <a href="/licenses" class="underline">Licenses</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>
